[RSTIB:migration] 2026-01-22 17:33:47 | INFO | Tool Task called with {'description': 'Adapt RSTIB model to LibCity', 'prompt': "Adapt the RSTIB model to LibCity conventions.\n\n**Context from repo-cloner analysis:**\n- Source repository: ./repos/RSTIB\n- Main model file: ./repos/RSTIB/methods/student/RSTIB_MLP.py\n- Supporting file: ./repos/RSTIB/methods/student/mlp.py\n- Engine/trainer: ./repos/RSTIB/engine.py (contains loss calculation logic)\n- Framework: PyTorch\n- Task type: Traffic speed prediction\n\n**Model Architecture Summary:**\n1. **RSTIB_MLP** uses:\n   - Time series embeddings (Conv2d: input_dim*lag → embed_dim)\n   - Node embeddings (learnable parameter)\n   - Temporal embeddings (time-of-day, day-of-week)\n   - Information Bottleneck encoder (MLP layers with reparameterization)\n   - Regression layer (Conv2d: hidden_dim//2 → horizon)\n   \n2. **MultiLayerPerceptron** component:\n   - Two Conv2d layers with residual connections\n   - ReLU activation, dropout (0.15)\n\n3. **Loss function** (from engine.py):\n   - Prediction loss (difficulty-weighted)\n   - Information bottleneck loss (KL divergence on mu/std)\n   - Multiple IB losses at different levels (encoding, output, reconstruction)\n\n**Your Tasks:**\n\n1. **Create LibCity model file**: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/RSTIB.py`\n   - Inherit from `AbstractTrafficStateModel`\n   - Implement `__init__(self, config, data_feature)`:\n     - Extract from data_feature: num_nodes, feature_dim, output_dim, scaler\n     - Extract from config: input_window, output_window, device, model hyperparameters\n   - Implement `forward(self, batch)`:\n     - Input: batch['X'] of shape (B, T_in, N, F)\n     - Extract temporal features from batch (time_of_day, day_of_week if available)\n     - Return predictions of shape (B, T_out, N, F)\n   - Implement `calculate_loss(self, batch)`:\n     - Prediction loss (MSE/MAE)\n     - Information bottleneck loss components (KL divergence)\n     - Return total loss (can simplify difficulty weighting for initial implementation)\n   - Implement `predict(self, batch)`:\n     - Call forward() and inverse transform with scaler if needed\n\n2. **Port the MLP component**:\n   - Include MultiLayerPerceptron class within RSTIB.py or as helper\n   - Maintain residual connections and dropout\n\n3. **Handle embeddings**:\n   - Node embeddings: learnable parameters\n   - Temporal embeddings: extract from batch or create as learnable\n   - LibCity provides time_of_day and day_of_week in batch if available\n\n4. **Simplifications allowed**:\n   - Skip knowledge distillation (teacher model) for initial version\n   - Skip difficulty weighting in loss (can be added later)\n   - Focus on core IB mechanism (reparameterization, KL loss)\n   - Use standard beta weight (0.001) without annealing\n\n5. **Register the model**:\n   - Add import to `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`\n   - Add to __all__ list\n\n**Key LibCity conventions to follow:**\n- Use `self.data_feature.get()` for dataset features\n- Use `config.get()` for hyperparameters with defaults\n- Use `self._scaler` for data normalization/denormalization\n- Use `self._logger` for logging (getLogger())\n- Device management: use `config.get('device')`\n\n**Reference**: Check existing models like STID or PatchTST in LibCity for structure examples.\n\nReport back with:\n1. Confirmation of file creation\n2. Any challenges encountered\n3. Hyperparameters added to config\n4. Whether model imports successfully", 'subagent_type': 'model-adapter'}
