[RSTIB:migration] 2026-01-22 18:17:12 | INFO | Tool Write called with {'file_path': '/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/RSTIB_bugfix_4_report.md', 'content': '# RSTIB Bug Fix #4: Encoder Dimension Mismatch\n\n## Bug Description\n\n**Issue**: When `if_dne=True` in config but DNE feature is unavailable at runtime, dimension mismatch occurs.\n\n**Error Message**:\n```\nRuntimeError: Given groups=1, weight of size [320, 320, 1, 1],\nexpected input[16, 256, 207, 1] to have 320 channels, but got 256 channels instead\n```\n\n**Root Cause**:\n- Initialization calculates `hidden_dim=320` assuming DNE will be present (64 channels for DNE)\n- Runtime skips DNE embedding when \'te\' key is missing in batch (due to Bug Fix #3)\n- Result: encoder expects 320 channels but receives only 256 channels\n\n**Expected Channels**: 320 = 64 (embed) + 64 (time_in_day) + 64 (day_in_week) + 64 (spatial) + 64 (DNE)\n**Actual Channels**: 256 = 64 (embed) + 64 (time_in_day) + 64 (day_in_week) + 64 (spatial) + **0 (DNE skipped)**\n\n## Solution Applied\n\n### Location\nFile: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/RSTIB.py`\nLines: 299-320\n\n### Changes Made\n\n**Before (Bug Fix #3 only)**:\n```python\n# Bug Fix #3: Robust batch key checking for DNE feature\nif self.if_dne:\n    try:\n        te = batch.get(\'te\') if hasattr(batch, \'get\') else batch.data.get(\'te\', None) if hasattr(batch, \'data\') else None\n        if te is not None:\n            dne = self.construct_dne(te.type(torch.LongTensor).to(self.device))\n            node_emb.append(dne)\n    except (KeyError, AttributeError) as e:\n        # DNE not available, skip\n        self._logger.debug(f"DNE feature skipped: {e}")\n        pass\n```\n\n**After (Bug Fix #3 + #4)**:\n```python\n# Bug Fix #3 & #4: Robust batch key checking for DNE feature with dimension consistency\nif self.if_dne:\n    try:\n        # Check if batch has \'te\' key via dictionary access\n        te = batch.get(\'te\') if hasattr(batch, \'get\') else batch.data.get(\'te\', None) if hasattr(batch, \'data\') else None\n        if te is not None:\n            dne = self.construct_dne(te.type(torch.LongTensor).to(self.device))\n            node_emb.append(dne)\n        else:\n            # Add zero-padding to maintain dimension consistency\n            B = history_data.shape[0]\n            N = history_data.shape[2]\n            zero_dne = torch.zeros(B, self.node_dim, N, 1, device=self.device)\n            node_emb.append(zero_dne)\n            self._logger.debug("DNE feature unavailable, using zero padding")\n    except (KeyError, AttributeError) as e:\n        # Add zero-padding on error to maintain dimension consistency\n        B = history_data.shape[0]\n        N = history_data.shape[2]\n        zero_dne = torch.zeros(B, self.node_dim, N, 1, device=self.device)\n        node_emb.append(zero_dne)\n        self._logger.debug(f"DNE feature skipped: {e}, using zero padding")\n```\n\n## Key Improvements\n\n1. **Dimension Consistency**: Zero-padding ensures encoder always receives expected 320 channels\n2. **Graceful Degradation**: Handles missing \'te\' key without crashing\n3. **Architecture Consistency**: Maintains consistency between initialization and forward pass\n4. **Proper Device Placement**: Uses `device=self.device` for correct device handling\n5. **Informative Logging**: Logs when zero-padding is used for debugging\n\n## Testing\n\nA test script has been created to verify the fix:\n- Location: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/test_rstib_import.py`\n- Tests:\n  1. Model import\n  2. Model instantiation with `if_dne=True`\n  3. Forward pass with missing \'te\' key (simulates bug scenario)\n  4. Output shape verification\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nWhen `if_dne=True` but \'te\' key is missing:\n- **Before Fix**: RuntimeError with dimension mismatch (256 vs 320 channels)\n- **After Fix**: Zero-padding added, model processes normally with 320 channels\n- Log message: "DNE feature unavailable, using zero padding"\n\n## Impact\n\n- **Backward Compatible**: Works with both old and new batch formats\n- **No Performance Impact**: Zero-padding is computationally negligible\n- **Robust**: Handles edge cases gracefully\n- **Maintains Model Logic**: DNE functionality preserved when \'te\' is available\n'}
