[DSTAGNN:migration] 2026-01-29 17:37:35 | INFO | Tool Bash called with {'command': "cat > /tmp/dstagnn_analysis.md << 'EOF'\n## Repository: DSTAGNN (Dynamic Spatial-Temporal Aware Graph Neural Network)\n\n### URL\nhttps://github.com/SYLan2019/DSTAGNN\n\n### Cloned Location\n./repos/DSTAGNN\n\n---\n\n## Key Files\n\n### Model Definition\n- **Main Model File**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/repos/DSTAGNN/model/DSTAGNN_my.py` (435 lines)\n  \n### Training Scripts\n- **Training Script**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/repos/DSTAGNN/train_DSTAGNN_my.py` (252 lines)\n- **Data Preparation**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/repos/DSTAGNN/prepareData.py` (12,560 bytes)\n\n### Configuration Files\n- **Config Files**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/repos/DSTAGNN/configurations/` (4 config files)\n  - PEMS03_dstagnn.conf\n  - PEMS04_dstagnn.conf\n  - PEMS07_dstagnn.conf\n  - PEMS08_dstagnn.conf\n\n### Utility Files\n- **Utils**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/repos/DSTAGNN/lib/utils.py` (585 lines)\n- **Utils1**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/repos/DSTAGNN/lib/utils1.py` (538 lines)\n- **Dataloader**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/repos/DSTAGNN/lib/dataloader.py` (48 lines)\n- **Metrics**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/repos/DSTAGNN/lib/metrics.py` (18 lines)\n- **Utility**: `/home/wangwenrui/shk/AgentCity/repos/DSTAGNN/lib/utility.py`\n\n---\n\n## Model Architecture Analysis\n\n### Main Model Classes\n\n1. **DSTAGNN_submodule** (Primary model class)\n   - Location: Lines 352-406 in DSTAGNN_my.py\n   - Inherits from: nn.Module\n   - Composition: Stack of DSTAGNN_block modules\n\n2. **DSTAGNN_block** (Core architectural block)\n   - Location: Lines 266-349 in DSTAGNN_my.py\n   - Key components:\n     - Temporal Attention (TAt): MultiHeadAttention layer\n     - Spatial Attention (SAt): SMultiHeadAttention layer\n     - Chebyshev Graph Convolution: cheb_conv_withSAt\n     - Gated Temporal Unit (GTU): Multiple GTU layers with varying kernel sizes (3, 5, 7)\n\n### Key Architectural Components\n\n#### Attention Mechanisms\n1. **MultiHeadAttention** (Lines 77-113)\n   - Scaled dot-product attention with residual connections\n   - Parameters: d_model, d_k, d_v, n_heads, num_of_d\n   - Output shape: [batch_size, num_of_d, len_q, d_model]\n\n2. **SMultiHeadAttention** (Lines 48-75)\n   - Spatial attention without value projection\n   - Returns attention scores only\n\n3. **ScaledDotProductAttention** (Lines 27-45)\n   - Core attention computation\n   - Includes residual attention matrix addition\n\n#### Graph Convolution\n1. **cheb_conv_withSAt** (Lines 116-173)\n   - K-order Chebyshev graph convolution\n   - Incorporates learned spatial attention masks\n   - Uses product attention matrix with adjacency matrix\n\n2. **cheb_conv** (Lines 176-224)\n   - Standard K-order Chebyshev convolution without attention\n\n#### Temporal Components\n1. **GTU (Gated Temporal Unit)** (Lines 249-262)\n   - Causal convolution with gating mechanism\n   - Uses tanh and sigmoid gates\n   - Three variants in DSTAGNN_block with kernels [3, 5, 7]\n\n2. **Embedding** (Lines 226-246)\n   - Positional embedding for temporal and spatial dimensions\n   - Etype: 'T' for temporal, 'S' for spatial\n\n### Model Factory Function\n- **make_model()** (Lines 408-435)\n  - Creates and initializes DSTAGNN_submodule\n  - Computes Chebyshev polynomials from adjacency matrix\n  - Xavier uniform initialization for weights\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies\n\n### Core Framework\n- **PyTorch**: torch, torch.nn, torch.nn.functional, torch.optim\n  - Version: Not explicitly specified, likely >= 1.0\n  \n### Scientific Computing\n- **NumPy**: numpy (array operations)\n- **Pandas**: pandas (data manipulation, CSV reading)\n- **SciPy**: scipy.sparse.linalg (eigenvalue decomposition), scipy.linalg (matrix operations)\n  \n### Machine Learning/Evaluation\n- **Scikit-learn**: sklearn.metrics (MAE, MSE, RMSE computation)\n\n### Visualization & Logging\n- **TensorBoard**: tensorboardX (training visualization and logging)\n- **Matplotlib**: matplotlib (visualization, used in utils.py)\n\n### Python Version\n- **Required**: Python >= 3.5 (as stated in README)\n- No Python 3.10+ specific features observed\n\n---\n\n## Data Format & Structure\n\n### Input Format\n- **Graph Signal Matrix**: NPZ files with keys:\n  - train_x: shape (B, N, F, T) where:\n    - B: batch size\n    - N: number of vertices/nodes\n    - F: features (typically 1 for traffic flow)\n    - T: time steps (input length = 12)\n  - train_target: shape (B, N, T_out) where T_out = 12\n  - val_x, val_target, test_x, test_target (similar structure)\n  - mean, std: normalization parameters\n\n### Adjacency Matrices\n1. **Base Adjacency Matrix** (PEMS04.csv format):\n   - CSV format, loaded via get_adjacency_matrix2()\n   - Represents road network connectivity\n   - Binary connectivity matrix\n\n2. **Spatial-Temporal Aware Graph (STAG)**:\n   - File: stag_001_PEMS04.csv\n   - Generated by STAG_gen.py from traffic data\n   - Input shape: (Total_Time_Steps, Node_Number)\n\n3. **Spatial-Temporal Relevance Graph (STRG)**:\n   - File: strg_001_PEMS04.csv\n   - Loaded via load_PA()\n   - Binary matrix after thresholding\n\n---\n\n## Configuration Parameters\n\n### Data Configuration (from PEMS04_dstagnn.conf)\n```\nadj_filename: path to adjacency matrix CSV\ngraph_signal_matrix_filename: path to NPZ data file\nstag_filename: spatial-temporal aware graph\nstrg_filename: spatial-temporal relevance graph\nnum_of_vertices: 307 (nodes in network)\nperiod: 288 (time steps per day, 12 * 24)\npoints_per_hour: 12\nnum_for_predict: 12 (prediction horizon)\nlen_input: 12 (input time window)\ndataset_name: PEMS04\n```\n\n### Training Configuration\n```\nctx: 0 (GPU device index)\nin_channels: 1 (input features)\nnb_block: 4 (number of DSTAGNN blocks)\nn_heads: 3 (attention heads for temporal attention)\nK: 3 (Chebyshev polynomial order, spatial attention heads)\nd_k: 32 (attention key/query dimension)\nd_model: 512 (embedding dimension)\nnb_chev_filter: 32 (Chebyshev filter channels)\nnb_time_filter: 32 (temporal filter channels)\nbatch_size: 32\ngraph: AG (use Spatial-Temporal Aware Graph vs regular adjacency)\nnum_of_weeks: 0\nnum_of_days: 0\nnum_of_hours: 1\nstart_epoch: 0\nepochs: 110\nlearning_rate: 0.0001\n```\n\n---\n\n## Training Pipeline\n\n### Data Loading\n1. **load_graphdata_channel1()** (lib/utils1.py):\n   - Loads preprocessed NPZ files\n   - Normalizes using z-score (mean/std)\n   - Creates PyTorch DataLoaders with batch_size\n   - Returns train/val/test loaders and normalization params\n\n2. **Adjacency Loading**:\n   - Base adjacency: get_adjacency_matrix2()\n   - STAG: load_weighted_adjacency_matrix()\n   - STRG: load_PA()\n\n### Model Training\n1. **Loss Function**: SmoothL1Loss\n2. **Optimizer**: Adam (learning_rate = 0.0001)\n3. **Validation**: compute_val_loss_mstgcn() - no learning rate scheduling\n4. **Best Model**: Saved based on validation loss\n5. **Metrics**: MAE, RMSE, MAPE (computed per time step)\n\n### Forward Pass\n- Input: (batch_size, num_vertices, num_features, num_timesteps)\n- Through DSTAGNN_block stack\n- Output: (batch_size, num_vertices, num_for_predict)\n\n---\n\n## Supported Datasets\n- PEMS03 (358 nodes)\n- PEMS04 (307 nodes)\n- PEMS07 (883 nodes)\n- PEMS08 (170 nodes)\n\nAll from STSGCN benchmark (AAAI-20)\n\n---\n\n## Key Implementation Details\n\n### Residual Attention Mechanism\n- Attention weights are accumulated across blocks (res_att parameter)\n- Spatial attention masks are learned (nn.Parameter) per K order\n- Masks combine with adjacency patterns: `myspatial_attention[:, k, :, :] + adj_pa.mul(mask)`\n\n### Temporal Convolution Strategy\n- Multiple GTUs with different kernel sizes (3, 5, 7)\n- Outputs concatenated: (3T-12) dimensions\n- Final FC layer projects back to T dimensions\n- Residual connections with input when multi-feature\n\n### Normalization\n- Input: Z-score normalization (mean subtraction, std division)\n- LayerNorm applied after residual connections in DSTAGNN_block\n- Output: Raw predictions (denormalized in evaluation)\n\n---\n\n## Notes for LibCity Migration\n\n1. **Module Structure**: Follows PyTorch nn.Module patterns cleanly\n2. **GPU Requirements**: Explicit .cuda() calls and DEVICE parameter throughout\n3. **Hyperparameter Heavy**: Many architectural choices (K, n_heads, d_model, etc.)\n4. **Attention Complexity**: Dual attention mechanisms (temporal + spatial)\n5. **Graph Processing**: Requires Chebyshev polynomial precomputation\n6. **Data Dependencies**: Expects preprocessed NPZ format with mean/std\n7. **No Submodules**: Repository is self-contained\n8. **Configuration**: Uses configparser (standard library)\n\nEOF\ncat /tmp/dstagnn_analysis.md\n", 'description': 'Create comprehensive analysis of DSTAGNN repository'}
