[LightST:migration] 2026-01-29 23:35:14 | INFO | Tool Task called with {'description': 'Fix LightST output shape', 'prompt': "Fix the output shape mismatch in the LightST model.\n\n**Issue Identified:**\n- File: `libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/LightST.py`\n- Line 515 in the `forward` method\n- Current code incorrectly transposes the output tensor twice\n- Result: Wrong shape `(B, 1, 12, 207)` instead of expected `(B, 12, 207, 1)`\n\n**Error Details:**\n```\nRuntimeError: The size of tensor a (12) must match the size of tensor b (207) at non-singleton dimension 2\n```\n\n**Required Fix:**\n\nChange line 515 from:\n```python\nreturn x.transpose(1, 3).transpose(2, 3)\n```\n\nTo:\n```python\nreturn x\n```\n\n**Explanation:**\nAfter `end_conv_2`, tensor `x` already has the correct shape `(B, 12, 207, 1)` which matches LibCity's expected format `(B, T_out, N, D_out)`. The double transpose was incorrectly moving dimensions around.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Before fix: Output shape is `(16, 1, 12, 207)` - WRONG\n- After fix: Output shape should be `(16, 12, 207, 1)` - CORRECT\n  - Dimension 0: Batch size (16)\n  - Dimension 1: Output time steps (12)\n  - Dimension 2: Number of nodes (207)\n  - Dimension 3: Output features (1)\n\nPlease apply this fix to the LightST.py file.", 'subagent_type': 'model-adapter'}
